From: =?UTF-8?q?Alperen=20Kele=C5=9F?= <alpkeles99@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 09:16:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(builtins): report printf's invalid numbers through the
 shell's stderr
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

printf left the parsing of numeric arguments to uucore, which reports a
bad one with `show_error!` on the process's fd 2 and records the failure in
its own global exit code. So `printf '%d\n' x 2>/dev/null` still printed
the message, and the status was 0 where bash returns 1.

Write the diagnostic to the builtin's stderr and return a failing status.

Signed-off-by: Alperen Keleş <alpkeles99@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5-5
